w-risk artifacts came from cmd-2c225df086e742c1 and cmd-cfebfd1aed584751. No failed services, new listening exposure, or package damage was observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-2c225df086e742c1","cmd-cfebfd1aed584751","global:after_prepare:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The mandatory node-restart protocol was also complete and coherent: it captured a healthy baseline, acknowledged the restart, showed a changed boot identity independently confirmed by lifecycle snapshots, and verified recovered system, timer, policy, log, and archive state. Only minor temporary test-file residue affects hygiene.","limitations":["Retention of exactly seven archives was verified through the installed policy and logrotate's parser rather than by executing enough rotations to exercise deletion of an eighth archive.","Open-writer continuity was tested with a representative file-descriptor-holding shell process because no inventory application service or process was present."]}
